  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new crate `crates/simview` (package `camcraft-simview`) holds the binary `camcraft-sim`. It has no edge to `camcraft-app` or `camcraft-ui`.\n- `camcraft-sim cl <file.cl> ...` is the old binary of the sim crate. It moved here with the same arguments, output and exit codes. Its three tests moved with it (`crates/simview/tests/check/cl_cmd.rs`).\n- `camcraft-sim check <file.nc> --stock <box> --tools <T map> (--post <.cps> | --dialect <name>) [--machine <.mch>] [--wcs G54=x,y,z]... [--fixture <box>]... [--cell <mm>]` is new. It parses the program with `camcraft-gcode` and runs these checks:\n  - post: the machine kind that the post serves, `programUnits`, `workOffsetMax` (manifest only, no hook runs);\n  - stock: a rapid through the material that is left, move by move in the field stock;\n  - holder law: the shank and holder bands against that material;\n  - fixture law: the region-free laws of `verify` over the `--fixture` boxes;\n  - machine limits: the #2585 judgment, in program coordinates;\n  - machine model: the spindle side against the work side of the generated model of #2584, at `work + --wcs`.\n- Exit codes: 0 each check ran and passed; 1 bad input; 2 a check failed (each finding names its NC line); 3 a check was not judged (each is named). 2 wins over 3.\n- A/B/C words refuse by name (the parser). An unmapped T refuses. A `.camtools` file refuses by name (follow-up #4465).\n- `camcraft-sim` drops its `tracing-subscriber` dependency (only the moved binary used it).\n- `xtask` lists `simview` in `BATCH_CRATES`, `ALL_CRATES` and `CLIPPY`, and its fixtures follow.\n- `docs/decisions/2574-standalone-camcraft-sim.md` records the #2574 research decisions and the crate edges with their imported items. `docs/decisions/2586-simview-check.md` records the decisions of this slice.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Cause\n\nThe maintainer asked for a stand-alone `camcraft-sim` (#2574). This is its first code slice.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in `crates/simview/tests/check/` (one directory suite, 13 tests):\n- `exits::check_exits_0_when_each_check_ran_and_passed`\n- `exits::check_exits_3_and_names_the_missing_machine_file`\n- `exits::check_exits_3_and_names_the_missing_work_offset`\n- `exits::check_exits_3_when_the_holder_stack_is_not_stated`\n- `exits::check_refuses_bad_input_with_exit_1` (missing file, an A word, a lathe machine, bad `--wcs`, bad dialect, no post, a bad box, `.camtools`, an unmapped T, no tools, no file)\n- `findings::check_names_the_line_of_a_travel_past_the_stroke`\n- `findings::check_names_the_line_of_a_machine_part_collision` (with the holder law finding)\n- `findings::check_names_the_line_of_a_rapid_through_material`\n- `findings::check_names_the_line_of_a_fixture_hit`\n- `catalog::check_runs_on_the_fanuc_catalog_program_for_the_default_vmc`: `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.nc` with `fanuc.cps` on `3axis-vmc.mch`. Exit 3: that machine file states no stroke and no part tree, and the closing G28 moves have no `--wcs`. Each is named. The stock and holder checks pass on the whole program.\n- `cl_cmd::*`: the old behaviour of the moved binary.\n\nRed before the change: yes. `upstream/main` has no `check` subcommand and no `camcraft-simview` package, so each pin fails.\n\nMutations (each guard disabled, its pin run, then restored; restored suite green, 13 passed):\n- not-judged exit code: red\n- limit judgment: red\n- machine-part collision: red\n- rapid through material: red\n- unmapped T refusal: red\n- holder law: red\n- fixture law: red\n\nGate on the final head (a4ee60c6b), against upstream/main 1cf7390dc: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` fell back to batch (the workspace manifest changed). Result: 1017 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, clippy included (wall 31.4 min).\n\nNew top-level test binary: `crates/simview/tests/check/` is the first suite of a new crate. The old binary test moved into it from `crates/sim/tests/sim_timeline/`.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-simview -p camcraft-sim -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n`cargo test -p xtask`: green.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No post, toolpath, golden or catalog program changes. The catalog program is read, not written. The example catalog suites are not reached.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\nNot run. This is a `P4` PR. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#3556) gives a heavy step only to a `P1` PR under the safety floor.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The window and playback (#2587), the job file (#2588), the button (#2589) and the release packages (#2590) are later slices.\n- A `.camtools` library (#4465).\n- 4- and 5-axis programs (#2592).\n- The machine model uses the generated bodies only. Its frame puts the spindle nose on the table top at joint zero (#2584). A real controller's machine zero is different, so a user gives `--wcs` in that frame.\n- G28 and G30 return to machine zero. A machine file that states another home is not read.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4383 and #4258 change the `members` line of the root `Cargo.toml` (a different entry). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: New `camcraft-sim check`: judges a posted 3-axis G-code file headless against a post, a machine file, the stock, the tools and the fixtures, with exit codes 0/1/2/3 and NC line numbers. The old headless stock simulation is now `camcraft-sim cl`.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #2586\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
